## 7. Evaluated Models

1. **Model A (Canonical XGBoost)**: 14 aggregate statistical features (bursts, packet sizes, IAT statistics, byte ratios).
2. **Model B1 (Lightweight Sequence Transformer)**: 4-feature packet sequence (Packet Length, Log-IAT, Direction, Position), max length = 32, 2 Transformer encoder layers (d_model=32, 2 heads).
3. **Model B2 (Protocol-Aware Sequence Transformer)**: Packet sequence + 4 deterministic protocol context markers appended to the sequence representation.
4. **Model B3 (Self-Supervised Pretrained Sequence Model)**: Pretrained via Masked Packet Length Reconstruction on the training fold, fine-tuned with a supervised classifier head.
5. **Model C (Hybrid Tabular + Sequence Classifier)**: Concatenation of Tabular View A (32-dim) and Sequence View B (32-dim) into a 64-dim representation with a classification head.
6. **Model D (Multi-View IPsec Classifier)**: Full multi-view fusion: Tabular View A (32-dim) + Sequence View B (32-dim) + Protocol Context View C (16-dim) = 80-dim representation projected to 48-dim.

