## 16. Research Summary

| Dimension | Outcome |
| :--- | :--- |
| **What Actually Improved** | **Hybrid Tabular + Sequence fusion (Model C)** achieved **80.25% Accuracy (+13.35% over XGBoost)** and **81.89% Macro-F1 (+7.98%)**, resolving the critical WEB vs INTERACTIVE classification bottleneck. Self-supervised pretraining (Model B3) also delivered a verified **+5.35%** gain. |
| **What Did Not Improve** | Appending static protocol context markers directly into small neural architectures (Models B2 & D) added redundant parameters without sufficient variance in a pure native-IPsec dataset, slightly degrading sample efficiency under strict capture splits. |
| **Recommended Next Step** | Integrate self-supervised pretraining into the Hybrid Model C architecture and evaluate open-set generalization on multi-protocol external VPN captures.
